import mundane theorem    stdlib/geometry/distance-by-coordinates
import mundane theorem    stdlib/geometry/between-by-coordinates

theorem a-midpoint-by-coordinates
  note        Both distances are worked out from the coordinates and come to
              the same number. M is between A and B because the vectors from
              M to A and to B are parallel and point opposite ways.
  let A be a point                                                    (H1)
  let B be a point                                                    (H2)
  let M be a point                                                    (H3)
  assume A = (−1, 1)                                                  (H4)
  assume B = (7, −4)                                                  (H5)
  assume M = (3, −3/2)                                                (H6)
  then |AM| = |MB|. M is between A and B.

1.  |(−1, 1)(3, −3/2)| = √((−1 − 3)² + (1 − (−3/2))²)
    mun:distance-by-coordinates

2.  |(3, −3/2)(7, −4)| = √((3 − 7)² + (−3/2 − (−4))²)
    mun:distance-by-coordinates

3.  |(−1, 1)(3, −3/2)| = |(3, −3/2)(7, −4)|
    calculation
      |(−1, 1)(3, −3/2)| = √((−1 − 3)² + (1 − (−3/2))²)      1
                         = √(89/4)                           arithmetic
                         = √((3 − 7)² + (−3/2 − (−4))²)      arithmetic
                         = |(3, −3/2)(7, −4)|                2

4.  |A(3, −3/2)| = |(3, −3/2)(7, −4)|
    substitute A = (−1, 1) (H4) into line 3

5.  |AM| = |M(7, −4)|
    substitute M = (3, −3/2) (H6) into line 4

6.  |AM| = |MB|
    substitute B = (7, −4) (H5) into line 5

7.  (−1 − 3)·(−4 − (−3/2)) = (7 − 3)·(1 − (−3/2))
    arithmetic

8.  (−1 − 3)·(7 − 3) + (1 − (−3/2))·(−4 − (−3/2)) < 0
    arithmetic

9.  (3, −3/2) is between (−1, 1) and (7, −4)
    mun:between-by-coordinates, from 7, 8

10. (3, −3/2) is between A and (7, −4)
    substitute A = (−1, 1) (H4) into line 9

11. M is between A and (7, −4)
    substitute M = (3, −3/2) (H6) into line 10

12. M is between A and B
    substitute B = (7, −4) (H5) into line 11

13. |AM| = |MB|. M is between A and B.
    join 6, 12
